    "narrative": "For the Zurich Zebras on August 25, 2026, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Junior Caminero** (74.78) emerge as our premier offensive engines. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits significantly from the matchup against Brandon Pfaadt, where his elite speed profile is bolstered by a +14% dynamic platoon advantage and a +4% bonus for a slow pitcher delivery, making him our highest-projected source for stolen bases today. **Junior Caminero** occupies a prime #3 slot against Jackson Jobe, leveraging a combination of park factors and favorable pitcher skill to anchor our production. **Yordan Alvarez** (73.61) remains a consistent force, with his elite 0.458 xwOBA providing the safest floor in the lineup, while **Lars Nootbaar** (62.07) finds value in a high-upside matchup against Clay Holmes, where a +11% platoon bump helps overcome the challenges of a middling opposing ERA.\n\nNavigating the bench required a close look at **Carson Benge** (36.49), who was the final omission from today\u2019s active squad. Despite a respectable base projection, the combination of a tough matchup against Kyle Harrison (xERA 3.05) and a significant -9% platoon penalty for the L/L matchup suppressed his efficiency score below our threshold, favoring the higher-ceiling utility of **Kazuma Okamoto** (59.97). While **Trea Turner** (61.15) and **Kyle Schwarber** (60.24) remain in the lineup due to their top-tier order placement, they face a legitimate test against George Kirby. Owners should monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all players, particularly **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith**; the latter\u2019s score (43.19) is particularly vulnerable to the L/L disadvantage against Ian Seymour. With **Casey Schmitt** and **Josh Smith** sidelined on the IL, our depth is currently prioritized toward maximizing stolen base opportunities and platoon-advantaged ABs over raw power in less favorable hitting conditions.",
